    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "freedom",
     "imagination",
     "work",
     "dignity"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The child admires people with different vocations, or jobs, such as hawker, gardener and watchman.\nHe sees only the freedom and the fun, because a child has limited ideas about real work.\nThe poem shows a child's imagination and wish to be free, but it also teaches us to notice the people who work around us.\nEvery honest job matters, which fits the unit's title, Work is Worship.\n(additional, not in the textbook) Respect people whatever their work."
    }
